G2634.definition:
κατα-κυριεύω  
 [in LXX:  Gen.1:28  (כָּבַשׁ),  Psa.110:2   Sir.17:4 , al. ;] 
 to gain or exercise dominion  (over); 
 __(a) absol. (Arist.); 
 __(b) with genitive (Arist., al.):  Mat.20:25 ,  Mrk.10:42 ,  Act.19:16 ,  1Pe.5:3 .†
   SYN. : (κατεξουσιάζω) (see Swete,  Mk. , l.with)   (AS)

G2675.definition:
κατ-αρτίζω  
 [in LXX chiefly in Ps ( Psa.8:2  al.; כּוּן, etc.) and Ezra (כְּלַל) ;] 
to render ἄρτιος, i.e. fit, complete; 
 __(a)  to mend, repair :  Mat.4:21 ,  Mrk.1:19 ; 
 __(b)  to furnish completely, complete, equip, prepare : pass.,  Luk.6:40 ,  Rom.9:22 ,  Heb.11:3 ; mid.,  Mat.21:16  (LXX),  Heb.10:5  (LXX); 
 __(with)  in ethical sense, to prepare, complete, perfect :  Gal.6:1  (EV, restore),  1Pe.5:10;  pass.,  1Co.1:10  (Field,  Notes , 167),  2Co.13:11 ,  Heb.13:21  (cf. προ-καταρτίζω).†
 (AS)
